<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:52:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine agree to major prisoner swap as peace talks end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c18d6fb9430270287e759f09612dfcf984abd30c977e05de8d830e7e4126fa35</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:46:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-and-ukraine-agree-to-major-prisoner-swap-as-peace-talks-end--e9c04d147348.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-and-ukraine-agree-to-major-prisoner-swap-as-peace-talks-end" /><summary type="html">Kyiv and Moscow on Wednesday agreed to a large-scale prisoner exchange as the final day of peace talks in Abu Dhabi came to an end, though neither side gave a concrete figure. US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner will meet separately with Russian President Vladimir Putin and his Ukrainian counterpart Volodymyr Zelensky on Thursday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Tshisekedi paves way for constitutional change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:393fe51aba411c24ea75a36c25f146e6f9775beac6813ae413ab327ad431cc0e</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:39:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tshisekedi-paves-way-for-constitutional-change--56435e73b5e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tshisekedi-paves-way-for-constitutional-change" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, A new law expanding the conditions for a constitutional referendum has ignited political tensions in the DRC. Also, Kenya has officially declared the end of its latest Ebola outbreak. And at COP31, environmental advocates are warning against waste incineration, arguing that it risks locking African cities into expensive and polluting infrastructure.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>General strike over housing brings out hundreds of thousands in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bf4121959c02abc01c09b436a217de0827dcb3b8774b1a36b028abe76a71148</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:31:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-hundreds-of-thousands-in-spain--305c14ca2c0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-hundreds-of-thousands-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Millions of workers in Spain shut down businesses and public transport on Wednesday, as part of the country's first general strike in 14 years. Following a peaceful march in Barcelona over soaring rents and property prices, and the rising cost of living, protesters smashed storefronts, set off small bonfires, burned bins and launched fireworks towards police. The unrest comes just weeks before snap elections, called by Socialist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rare Marilyn Monroe photos from her final shoot to be auctioned</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d5f1b3b07c6fb5c547e64ebf5618af0d01a731ca23a6fe7f3130b5375f6ec59</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:05:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/rare-marilyn-monroe-photos-from-her-final-shoot-to-be-auctioned--12329e4a8531.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rare-marilyn-monroe-photos-from-her-final-shoot-to-be-auctioned" /><summary type="html">Prints from the personal collection of renowned photographer Bert Stern, including his celebrated series The Last Sitting of Marilyn Monroe, are set to be auctioned at Gros &amp; Delettrez in Paris, marking the first such sale of Stern's private archives. At the heart of the Dec. 2 auction is The Last Sitting, a series of photographs taken in June and July 1962 at the Hotel Bel-Air in Los Angeles, just weeks before Monroe's death. FRANCE 24's Olivia Bizot reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>France turns back Israeli settler representative upon arrival in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65d338559cc40d2afdfb788b90e7305d5b8f1c510e79794b1daa5249f7942f0e</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T20:58:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261111-france-turns-back-israeli-settler-representative-upon-arrival-in-paris--737b9da8fdc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261111-france-turns-back-israeli-settler-representative-upon-arrival-in-paris" /><summary type="html">French authorities forced Samaria Regional Council head Yossi Dagan to leave the country after he landed at a Paris airport last week, his office said in a statement on Wednesday. The French foreign ministry did not confirm his deportation, only saying that Dagan was banned from French territory due to his involvement in Israel's illegal settlements in the occupied West Bank.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>RSF calls for release of French reporter Christophe Gleizes, detained in Algeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a11b5d78273e93c8391a4a31971bf160c28e92b6fde96b1c8c36a2d0a3e23867</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T20:44:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/rsf-calls-for-release-of-french-reporter-christophe-gleizes-detained-in-algeria--eb9bfb7ed051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rsf-calls-for-release-of-french-reporter-christophe-gleizes-detained-in-algeria" /><summary type="html">After being detained for almost 500 days in Algeria, Christophe Gleizes is no closer to being freed. Those close to him, as well as his fellow sports journalists have campaigned tirelessly for his release with the affair even attracting the attention of Zinedine Zidane, manager of the French football team. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Thibault Bruttin, Director General of Reporters Without Borders. He says that Gleizes has probably become "a token in a diplomatic game that we don't totally understand, that we don't totally master, up to the point where we are asking ourselves 'has he become a state hostage?'".</summary></entry><entry><title>General strike over housing brings out tens of thousands in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1ce802466e80da7149e07d0d4920a05473a25419446deb112d9f2bb3a1406cf</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:37:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-tens-of-thousands-in-spain--b3f1fe2dfc35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-tens-of-thousands-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of protesters marched across Spain on Wednesday during a general strike over housing affordability and purchasing power just weeks before an early general election. Unions reported a significant response in some sectors in Spain's first nationwide 24-hour stoppage since 2012, but business leaders played down the participation. Braving heavy rain, tens of thousands of demonstrators marched through central Madrid carrying placards shaped like houses and chanting "We have no home" as they called for more affordable housing. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Undone by a honey trap? Nvidia's Jensen Huang at heart of China spy scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fced18b9ef0979a41626172f7f9ea95b4d536ca70ae26ceeb4b8a041deb898c7</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:32:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261111-undone-by-a-honey-trap-nvidia-s-jensen-huang-at-heart-of-china-spy-scandal--ef71664cdb96.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261111-undone-by-a-honey-trap-nvidia-s-jensen-huang-at-heart-of-china-spy-scandal" /><summary type="html">Turns out that the new masters of the universe are human, all too human. China accused of exploiting a vulnerability at the heart of the Silicon Valley giant that reigns supreme over two-thirds of the planet’s AI computing power production, the Nvidia co-founder tempted by the flesh. Jensen Huang admitting to an extramarital affair with Singapore-based Chinese tech CEO Alice Huang - no relation. She’s under scrutiny over the purchase of Nvidia state-of-the-art chips that may have been smuggled back to the mainland illegally. We’ll ask about the rise and possible fall of the Taiwan-born leather-clad AI world icon.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands attend Polish nationalist march days after shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13716cec034eceae83266b2278b88a76526bf05c9f087560565656f9b2ef5526</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:31:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings-1--6aff4f4e4234.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings-1" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of Polish nationalist sympathisers gathered in Warsaw Wednesday for an annual Independence Day March, just days after a deadly shooting spree in Krakow that shook the country. The event is held each November 11 to commemorate the ending in 1918 of 123 years of partition by Russia, Prussia and Austria. The event is a magnet for all shades of Poland's right wing -- from conservative-nationalists aligned with its Law and Justice (PiS) party to far-right and radical groups. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Schools evacuated across Italy after bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d8a9e3cf89a32f76f487a42138123d7a1d98b22073f55020ad1550752c62dd4</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:29:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/schools-evacuated-across-italy-after-bomb-threats--8b8597a1d133.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/schools-evacuated-across-italy-after-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Schools were evacuated across Italy on Wednesday following a series of hoax bomb threats, but Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni said there was no "concrete danger". Similar hoax threats were reported in schools in Britain and Ireland, which reportedly prompted some evacuations in Scotland. Meloni said she had called a government meeting with security and intelligence chiefs for Wednesday to discuss the threats. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia's Jensen Huang at heart of China spy scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82e947a84e2a3ad2f56a20054e7d6958f3dacb71de7c21caeef1006b8947e2dd</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:23:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261111-nvidia-s-jensen-huang-at-heart-of-china-spy-scandal--b2d1ba9983fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261111-nvidia-s-jensen-huang-at-heart-of-china-spy-scandal" /><summary type="html">Turns out that the new masters of the universe are human, all too human. China accused of exploiting a vulnerability at the heart of the Silicon Valley giant that reigns supreme over two-thirds of the planet’s AI computing power production, the Nvidia co-founder tempted by the flesh. Jensen Huang admitting to an extramarital affair with Singapore-based Chinese tech CEO Alice Huang - no relation. She’s under scrutiny over the purchase of Nvidia state-of-the-art chips that may have been smuggled back to the mainland illegally. We’ll ask about the rise and possible fall of the Taiwan-born leather-clad AI world icon.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>The most hacked country in Europe? Why is France the target of so many cyberattacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f9f513e6efda7e461af46a52f4a7eb268742f02891fdcebadbbfb8ae54a113f</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:09:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261111-the-most-hacked-country-in-europe-why-is-france-the-target-of-so-many-cyberattacks--b6425f1872a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261111-the-most-hacked-country-in-europe-why-is-france-the-target-of-so-many-cyberattacks" /><summary type="html">The “unprecedented” hacks of French supermarket refrigerators were the latest in a series of major cyberattacks that have made the country the most hacked in Europe, according to some analysts. Cyberattacks are on the rise globally, but why is France such a ready target?</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands attend Polish nationalist march days afer shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7726f1f1eaf360ae8772f2ff76963756a107d01a9564b5e5a40b9bc067313db</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:08:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings--f224bca0510d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of Polish nationalist sympathisers gathered in Warsaw Wednesday for an annual Independence Day March, just days after a deadly shooting spree in Krakow that shook the country. The event is held each November 11 to commemorate the ending in 1918 of 123 years of partition by Russia, Prussia and Austria. While generally peaceful, some rallies in the pasthave been marred by clashes with police or counter-demonstrators. Philip Turle gives us his take.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tehran will strike US bases in Europe if used to attack Iran, security chief says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da7b35748e0e6349ace1ca5add4950bc2f3737bdde0230ce759a69e810272b9b</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:45:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261111-tehran-will-strike-us-bases-in-europe-if-used-to-attack-iran-security-chief-says--80ef79332bde.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261111-tehran-will-strike-us-bases-in-europe-if-used-to-attack-iran-security-chief-says" /><summary type="html">Iranian security chief Mohsen Rezaei said Wednesday that Tehran would attack US bases located in Europe if they were used to carry out bombing raids against the Islamic republic. The heavy defeat of US President Donald Trump's Republican Party in the midterm elections earlier this month seems to have pushed Washington to pull back its threats to carry out fresh strikes against Iran.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Haiti: 'We need to know the truth, but so far, it’s totally dark'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db7f8a87c553fd1ac2c0000bf457c5a21e492b3c82db89366664dc82f4da0039</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:52:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:38:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bukele-says-salvadoran-troops-destroyed-gang-hq-in-haiti--a7661e77071f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bukele-says-salvadoran-troops-destroyed-gang-hq-in-haiti" /><summary type="html">Jean-Marie Théodat, Director of the Department of Geography at University Paris, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Violent incidents in schools as French students vow to maintain protest pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d66be1b0c72f98e8a95f33cf18a5372e92b772e1e98df3b9991fe56d46724c90</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:52:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:35:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/violent-incidents-in-schools-as-french-students-vow-to-maintain-protest-pressure--54d6bee3daef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/violent-incidents-in-schools-as-french-students-vow-to-maintain-protest-pressure" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Tuesday condemned violence against teachers andgovernment officials during nationwide street protests after an official was hit by a gasoline-filled bottle outside ​a high school ‌near Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil electoral court fines Meta $1.3 MN, sees no deliberate election bias</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6114101f5ec75fd187cea5940f1cce044791d411cb21a77316a518f11a267154</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:08:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-1-3-mn-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias--81c14c584e59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-1-3-mn-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias" /><summary type="html">Jan Onoszko, our correspondent in Rio, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31 talks in Turkey: Leaders from US, China and India skip summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:049f4a79386190f6f07dd07285da13ac1b1393f0182738f28a7e463ba294a9bd</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:52:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:06:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/cop31-talks-in-turkey-leeaders-from-us-china-and-india-skip-summit--1f44812cc455.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cop31-talks-in-turkey-leeaders-from-us-china-and-india-skip-summit" /><summary type="html">Valérie Dekimpe, our environment editor, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>President Macron speaks for Armistice Day commemoration ceremony</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f517d985349ab3b6a131d10e6ce029b4f65e4245980084e589caa5ba1695a7af</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:52:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:03:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/president-macron-speaks-for-armistice-day-commemoration-ceremony--f4f0d2f60dd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/president-macron-speaks-for-armistice-day-commemoration-ceremony" /><summary type="html">On Wednesday, Emmanuel Macron presided over his final Armistice Day ceremony in Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia bans two French lawmakers and two journalists from entry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9226846459234ddde32857ebcacdaa36aee09f517001a6ac6b9eae0a7c0aae3f</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:58:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry--647f8165ba44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry" /><summary type="html">Moscow on Wednesday said it was banning two French journalists and two French lawmakers from entering Russia in response to Paris's expulsion of pro-Russian TV commentator Xenia Fedorova earlier this year.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Armistice Day in France: Macron honors the End of World War I</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df696fcf221ca9d415ee8f64c7df11a858745aebcaa9c0f6c3c7f4810447305</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:57:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-armistice-day-in-france-commemorating-the-end-of-world-war-i--1302880ba7fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261111-armistice-day-in-france-commemorating-the-end-of-world-war-i" /><summary type="html">With less than six months to go before the presidential election, the 11 November commemorations have taken on a political hue. On Wednesday, Emmanuel Macron presided over his final ceremony in Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: General strike over housing costs before national election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dcaafcf1068f1db6ee2384df09376dc27fd0bd3ae1103f9bc1cae60b5da006c</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:54:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election--d795ce513ad5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election" /><summary type="html">Millions of Spanish workers shut down businesses and public transportation in a protest on Wednesday over housing costs that the government hopes to leverage before a national election later this month. The walkout — under the slogan “Salaries. Housing. Prices.” — was the first general strike in Spain in 14 years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Exclusive: EU's Kallas says US 'can't negotiate on our behalf' on lifting Russia sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c0c3f2435a61381cf6f1fdf44d5f020466807a554c3598e92403d69de40b93b</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions--7f31e05dcc4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions" /><summary type="html">In an exclusive interview with FRANCE 24, the EU's top diplomat Kaja Kallas discusses the war in Ukraine, the situation in the Middle East and a possible change in US President Donald Trump's foreign policy following the US midterm elections. The former Estonian prime minister, who is now the European Union's High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy, also reaffirms the EU's position as a major player on the global geopolitical stage.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Charlotte Gainsbourg brings pioneering French lawyer Gisèle Halimi to the screen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b9f96dc4f03354991cef5423d35501171fa18de73e81f212cbcd439a706f69b</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:13:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261111-charlotte-gainsbourg-brings-pioneering-french-lawyer-gis_le-halimi-to-the-screen--15609dd4243d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261111-charlotte-gainsbourg-brings-pioneering-french-lawyer-gis%C3%A8le-halimi-to-the-screen" /><summary type="html">New French film "Women on trial" revisits the landmark case in 1972 that paved the way for abortion legislation in France. Critic Manon Kerjean tells us why performances from Charlotte Gainsbourg and Cécile de France carry this powerful courtroom drama and how its directors recreated the tension of a high-profile social and legal battle.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry></feed>
